From: Khanh Truong <khanhtd36@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 14:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] vendor(libghostty-vt): add cursor_is_at_prompt and
 cursor_home C API

Export two new FFI functions:

- ghostty_terminal_cursor_is_at_prompt(): a thin wrapper around the
  existing Terminal.cursorIsAtPrompt() (already used internally by real
  Ghostty's own clear_screen keybind action), so callers can detect
  whether the cursor is sitting at an idle, shell-integration-reported
  prompt before deciding to redraw it.
- ghostty_terminal_cursor_home(): moves the primary screen's cursor to
  (0, 0), always targeting the primary screen regardless of which
  screen is active, matching ghostty_terminal_clear_screen()'s
  primary-screen targeting.

Vendored base: c5a21edfcbc2d5b46540ad91b7980aca31f5f1f3
